      "Add a compact grouped Claude writer-development entry on each matching project Storyboard page, with useful scene-card/story/series links; preserve preliminary Grok visual groups and already registered sequences. Provide the source text access and related panel/character links rather than an unrelated new top-level app.",
      "Separate music-video development from standalone stories/series. Link writing and research context through the existing documents/collaborator views where appropriate; keep proposed character ideas distinct from accepted illustrated cast.",
      "Make latest VALIS revision discoverable as research/story-development context. The current 16241-byte revision supersedes the older cited 14725-byte snapshot. Never replace its source or silently treat six proposals as accepted canon.",
      "Update durable site sources and use the existing single-owner builder. Snapshot current canonical reviews/scopes/selections/source bytes and song/timing records; test relevant routing/links and preservation. Report actual publication links and limits.",
      "Return concise reconciliation report, source/placement checkpoint and preservation evidence. Keep standing ownership after completion."
    ],
    "preservationRules": [
      "Do not edit Claude-authored documents or coordinator-owned production records merely to make them agree with display.",
      "Preserve exact old review IDs, notes, ratings, explicit clears, favorites, basket, histories and scopes; do not seed accepted timing, new actor canon or generation readiness.",
      "Older writer holds and next actions may be dated; reconcile with current production method and actual accepted references. Surface unresolved conflicts instead of resetting settled acceptance or copying obsolete holds as current instructions.",
      "Do not promote research-labelled or draft work into production sources. Calibration answer keys/control payloads need no front-page exposure; use appropriate workflow records only.",
      "No provider/generator execution, spend, source selection, public deployment or media regeneration in this site task.",
      "Respect existing local-browser visual QA policy limitation; static/DOM checks must be labelled accurately."
    ],
